Do not crash in ar tv when ctime() fails.
header_verbose_list_ar() edits the string from ctime() without checking
for NULL, which ctime() returns when the time is out of range. That
happens on Windows for times after the year 3000, so a damaged or
crafted archive member crashed "ar tv". Print question marks instead.

---
 archival/ar.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/archival/ar.c
+++ b/archival/ar.c
@@ -215,10 +215,13 @@
 {
 	const file_header_t *file_header = archive_handle->file_header;
 	char mode[12];
+	char bad_mtime[] = "??? ??? ?? ??:??:?? ????\n";
 	char *mtime;
 
 	bb_mode_string(mode, file_header->mode);
 	mtime = ctime(&file_header->mtime);
+	if (!mtime) /* out of range */
+		mtime = bad_mtime;
 	mtime[16] = ' ';
 	memmove(&mtime[17], &mtime[20], 4);
 	mtime[21] = '\0';
